e":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.2507111756107866,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.006541595572377467,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":56.5,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.00022149868259821294,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":10.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.11640750727394455,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.1220570012391573,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.12619,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":84.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.083,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":8.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Precigen, Inc.,a discovery and clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, develops gene and cell therapies using precision technology to target diseases in areas of immuno-oncology, autoimmune disorders, and infectious diseases. The company offers therapeutic platforms consisting of AdenoVerse platform, which utilizes a library of proprietary adenovectors for gene delivery of therapeutic effectors, immunomodulators, and vaccine antigen; and UltraCAR-T to provide chimeric antigen receptor T cell therapies for cancer patients. It also develops programs based on the UltraCAR-T platform, including PRGN-3005 in Phase 1/1b clinical trial to treat advanced ovarian, fallopian tube, or primary peritoneal cancer; PRGN-3006 in Phase 1b trial for patients with relapsed or refractory acute myeloid leukemia and high-risk myelodysplastic syndromes; and PRGN-3007 in Phase 1/1b trial for the treatment of advanced receptor tyrosine kinase-like orphan receptor 1-positive, hematologic, and solid tumors. In addition, the company is developing programs based on the AdenoVerse immunotherapy platform comprising PRGN-2009 in Phase 2 trial for patients with HPV+ solid tumors; and PRGN-2012 in Phase \u00bd trial to treat recurrent respiratory papillomatosis. Further, it provides UltraPorator, a proprietary electroporation device. The company was formerly known as Intrexon Corporation and changed its name to Precigen, Inc. in February 2020. Precigen, Inc. was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Germantown, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Helen  Sabzevari MPH, Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 160 people. Revenue per employee of $61K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, declining at 7%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 34\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Precigen, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $10M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -55% over the past three years and -25% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -57% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $90M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -104.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -28.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 112% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-15.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 1141% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 165% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.6456885456885457},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (92% sell ratio, net $6.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 82/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as in